# Cloudflare Pages security headers — applied to every response.
# Conservative on purpose: nothing here blocks a CDN, RPC, worker, camera (QR),
# geolocation (maps) or wallet popup the app already uses. CSP is limited to the
# three directives that are safe without a build step (no script/connect limits,
# which would need per-file nonces the static site can't maintain).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Permissions-Policy: browsing-topics=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self' https://preview.ost-studio.invalid

# OST Studio keeps projects and the mesh identity in first-party storage, so no page
# (not even an OST page showing a user-made app) may frame it. A second CSP header is
# a second policy that is enforced too, so frame-ancestors 'none' wins over 'self'.
# The preview.ost-studio.invalid base above is Studio's sandboxed preview: srcdoc
# frames inherit this policy, and the preview sets <base href> to that never-resolving
# host so relative URLs inside a project can be intercepted.
/studio
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
/studio.html
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
/coding-studio
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
/coding-studio.html
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
